  "notes": "The live-instrument-plus-sampler end of the lane, and the research's headline claim is a *layer count*: \"his records have the highest layer count in this section; countermelody is a real second instrument.\" That is the parameter this model actually carries — `countermelody.densityRatio` 0.65 with `fillGapsOnly` false and three answering styles, which is the densest counter in this batch outside the live band. His named gear is the **Ensoniq ASR-10** and **Propellerhead Reason**, which the research reads as \"crunchy 12/16-bit drum timbre and step-sequenced programming\": `quantizeStrength` 0.70 with real jitter on the hats, `snare.layered` and `rimshotLayer` both true, ghost notes at 0.30 across three positions, and \"16th hats with light swing\" at 0.55. Harmony is the second identity — \"suspended and added-note chords, string-derived harmony, `i–VI–III–VII` and `i–iv–VII`, 4- and 8-bar loops with real motion\" — so `susSubstitutionProb` is 0.30, 70% of `extensions` is above the triad, `phraseBars` reaches 8, and `structure` is `long_arc` rather than a riff loop. The bass is played, not an 808: \"prefers played/sampled bass with a sub layer underneath rather than a naked 808; lines move melodically under the changes\" is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.45 with walking cells, while `bass808.role` drops to `counter_riff`. ⚠ `medium`: the research is medium-high on gear and role but says \"specific tempo habits inferred from placements **[LOW-CONF]**\". The INFERRED parameters are the whole `session.bpm` band and the kick's `secondaryAnchor` — \"a syncopated pickup\" names no position, and `2a` is one reading of it. ⚠ The 130-140 half-time population is documented and not modeled (one `halfTime` boolean, no modes authored). ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.35 to 0.61.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.35 over this model's 8-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The chord voicing moved up to [51, 91] so the bass stays under the harmony — it started at 44 against a bass reaching 50, an overlap of 7. The span is preserved; a voicing that low was competing with the bass rather than sitting over it. ⚠ `countermelody.fillGapsOnly` returned to true. With it off and a density of 0.65, the counter plays THROUGH the melody rather than around it, and coherence.rs measures that as the counter sounding the melody own pitch at the same moment — a second lead rather than an answer. The register offset and the styles are untouched; what changed is that it waits its turn.",
